00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:03.060
A useful tool within Word is
the find and replace tool.

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:07.170
This allows you to search through
a document for a specific word, and

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:08.400
then replace it with another word.

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:12.000
This could be very useful if you
have a large document and you need

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.490
to find instances of a word that
may appear a hundred, 200 times

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:18.620
and it needs to be changed quickly.

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:22.850
As an example, I have a letter on
the screen and I'm going to use

00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:27.069
the find and replace tool to change
the word "data" to "information".

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.330
There are several instances
of the word "data".

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:34.390
And so I click on the
editing tool, select replace.

00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:39.680
And the word I'm looking for
is "data" and I'm going to

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:43.340
replace that with "information".

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:47.910
There are three options here, so
you can replace, and that will

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:50.250
replace each instance one at a time.

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:54.180
So you can just confirm that this is
okay, or you can select replace all.

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:58.560
This will automatically search through the
whole document and replace every instance

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:00.480
of the word data with information.

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:04.570
It's good to be careful with
this because there may be certain

00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:06.390
words are part of other words.

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:10.030
An example of this is
"night-time"/"nightmare".

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:15.765
So if you are looking to change the word
"night"into something else and those

00:01:15.765 --> 00:01:18.525
words were present in that document,
it would automatically change the

00:01:18.525 --> 00:01:23.025
first part of that word into whatever
you had decided to change it into.

00:01:24.045 --> 00:01:27.225
So for this one here, I'm just going
to change data with information

00:01:27.975 --> 00:01:32.085
and I'll go through one at a  time
so if I select replace, as you can

00:01:32.085 --> 00:01:33.525
see, it's highlighted the word data.

00:01:33.525 --> 00:01:34.815
So I click replace.

00:01:36.255 --> 00:01:41.455
The second instance has appeared, click,
replace, and replace, and replace . Word

00:01:41.455 --> 00:01:45.204
has now finished searching the document
and I can close that . And every

00:01:45.204 --> 00:01:49.404
instance of the word "data" has been
replaced with the word "information".

